Z||000000||jelly2m8||10-23-2001||07:33 PM||||Hi guys,<P> I'm going to be picking up a Fiero in Orlando FL, and driving it back to Nova Scotia.<P>I'm just wondering if there is anybody along the eastern seaboard that would be willing to help out in case I run into trouble along the way. IE:, breakdowns, rest stops, info, stuff like that. <P> The time frame looks to be anywhere from October 30th, to the 3rd week in November. I'm just debating on flying down on the 30th, or wait untill the 9th of November, and hitch a ride to Florida with a customer of mine.<P> I might have to do this drive solo, and it would be nice to have some possible help along the way. You can reply here, or send me E-mail if you are interested.<P> I will have more solid plans come this weekend.<P>Thanks<P>A Cook<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever3000||10-23-2001||07:44 PM||||Wow.  I recommend going to <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/cgi-local/foldinstructions.htm" TARGET=_blank>FOLD</A> and pulling up some of the cities along the way. Then email those people before the trip, because FOLD is not 100% up-to-date.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||10-23-2001||08:05 PM||||Hey Anthony, You can depend on us for food and shelter and anything else you might need.  If you would be here on Nov. 4th you could spend the day with us on the Fall Fiero Meeting and cruise.  <P>For those out there that do not know Anthony let me tell you a little about him.  Last summer we took a trip to Nova Scotia.  We posted in the forum of our intentions and asked who we might meet that had Fieros.  We had a great invitation from Anthony to visit him while in Nova Scotia.  When we got there, we  meet the nicest Fiero enthusist you could ever meet.  Anthony runs his own garage to repair and restore Fieros.  He works on Fieros from all over eastern Canada.  We stayed with Anthony for two days.  He was going to a car show the one day and he took three of his Fieros and allowed us to drive one to the show.  He took us on a Fiero cruise of the area to show us the sites and local food.  We met many of his Fiero buddies and checked out their cars.  He even let me take his V8 Fiero out for a spin. WOW.  Anyway I just wanted everyone to know this is really a great guy that you will be glad you met.  Please give him a hand if you can.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||10-23-2001||08:22 PM||||If your driving through RI on I-95, honk your horn as you pass exit 6 (Rt. 3)||||reg||1
Z||000004||California Kid||10-23-2001||08:30 PM||||jelly2m8:  Have a safe swweeeet trip!!! Remember to pull over when "white line fever" kicks in, tired mind will do real strange things to ya. Wish I could help you out, I'm just a little too far west.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
